   Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; TU Bergakademie Freiberg},
Abstract = {Serious traffic congestion appears during the development of urban
   transportation in China. Traffic problems have produced many adverse
   effects on people' lives, partly because of an inadequate investment in
   transport infrastructure and a lag of green transportation in many
   cities. The paper tries to put forward some solutions by summarizing the
   current transport characteristics in different cities and analyzing the
   causes. Hopefully, these methods can have some value in decision-making
   to develop green transportation in line with low-carbon economy for the
   Chinese government, which include scientific planning of city layout,
   building multi-level public transportation systems, adjusting traffic
   through price, restricting private cars and promoting green traffic idea
   among the public.},
