   Dispersion Modelling for Regulatory Purposes, Paris, FRANCE, JUN 01-05,
   2010},
Abstract = {This study explores for the first time, the applicability of the Danish
   Operational Street Pollution Model (OSPM) in the city of Buenos Aires
   where street canyons are very irregular. The model is applied in an
   irregular and asymmetric street canyon of a five-lane avenue near a
   street intersection. Urban background concentrations estimated by the
   DAUMOD model are considered. Meteorological information registered at
   the domestic airport located in the city is used in calculations. Three
   months of hourly NOx, NO2 and CO estimated concentrations are compared
   with measurements inside the street canyon. Statistical evaluation of
   model results shows that OSPM performance is quite good.},
