Abstract = {Discovering how emotions influence consumers retention is crucial.
   Companies who generate strong emotional association with their customers
   can fulfil and capture their unconscious feelings. The emotionally
   connected customers will be more motivated to continue buying from the
   company. Objective: To investigate how emotional motivation affect
   customer loyalty behaviours by testing the relationship between peer
   group pressure, self-esteem and retention for Halal cosmetics. Methods:
   We looked at the relative on customer retention from 359 different
   respondents across 6 different states in Malaysia using 5-points Likert
   scale questionnaire. Result: Positive relationship between peer group
   pressure, self-esteem and retention were identified using PLS analysis.},
