   patterns of indoor air perception obtained by principal component
   analysis, using an visual analogue scale. At 18 degrees C, in the
   Rhinitis group, there was a correlation between dryness, stagnant air,
   and difficult mental concentration. This group also correlated heat, dry
   air, and bad indoor air quality, in opposition to the Control group,
   which correlated well-being, easy mental concentration, and freshness.
   At 22 degrees C, the Rhinitis group correlated heat, dryness, stagnant
   indoor air perception, and overall discomfort. This group also
   correlated non-dry air, freshness, and well-being. The Control group
   correlated heat.. humidity, good indoor air, freshness and well-being.
   This study suggests that the Rhinitis group perceives indoor
   temperatures of 18 degrees C and 22 degrees C as dryer and more adverse
   than controls do.},
