Abstract = {Within the framework of this paper, the impact of various transport
   demand management (TDM) strategies, designed for urban central areas, to
   fuel consumption is examined and evaluated through the use of the
   traffic simulation and assignment model SATURN. TDM strategies examined
   include high occupancy vehicle (HOV) lanes, bus lanes (with flow and
   contra-flow) and schemes for pedestrian-only streets and bus-only
   streets. The modeling results have been quite encouraging, in most
   cases.},
