Year = {1999},
Volume = {3},
Pages = {283-288},
Note = {XIVth Annual International Occupational Ergonomics and Safety Conference
   1999, ORLANDO, FL, JUN 06-09, 1999},
Abstract = {NCAA studies indicate that women soccer athletes have the highest rate
   of ACL injury of all intercollegiate athletes. This type injury often
   requires reconstructive surgery. The purpose of this research was to
   determine the perceptions of the athlete, coach, trainer, and physician
   regarding the success of the surgery and to also determine risk factors
   associated with ACL injuries. Results indicated that the elected surgery
   technique does not significantly determine overall success. However, the
   physician's perception of the surgery's success is significantly higher
   than that of the athletes. Risk factors include type of playing surface,
   time during competition, and the season's duration. Those programs that
   emphasize total body conditioning had fewer injuries. To reduce risk,
   physical conditioning programs should emphasize the strengthening of all
   muscle groups as well as aerobic conditioning.},
