   MELBOURNE, AUSTRALIA, APR 07-12, 2002},
Organization = {Int Water Assoc},
Abstract = {This paper describes a probability-based method for assessing the
   potential impact of climate change on urban water supply systems.
   Specifically, the assessment method uses probability distributions to
   place a confidence level on the plausible values of response variables.
   The Benalla water supply system has been used to demonstrate
   applicability of the proposed assessment method. For the application,
   the impact of the 2030 climate change scenarios on streamflows and
   system yield has been examined. The preliminary results have
   demonstrated that the proposed assessment method can provide valuable
   insights into the impact of climate change on water supply systems,
   allowing it to be incorporated into planning decisions.},
