   Munich, GERMANY, AUG 25-26, 2018},
Organization = {TU Bergakademie Freiberg; Tianjin Univ Finance \& Econ, Tourism Dept;
   German Acad Exchange Serv Fdn; IMRE Alumni Network},
Abstract = {The rapid development of hospitality industry in last three decades,
   hotel industry has become an important business sector in China. Being a
   responsible cooperate, socially and environmental, is now accepted by
   many hotels. The research aims to explore the perception of CRS in
   luxury hotels in China from guests' perspective and discuss if CSR can
   affect guests' decision making when they select a luxury hotel. 21
   interviewees from China, who had luxury hotel experiences, were
   interviewed. It was found that guests' perception of luxury hotels' CSR
   activities are concentrated on environmental conservation, charity
   donation and community support. People who are frequently travelers and
   fewer prices sensitive have started to concern about CSR and put it into
   their consideration when selecting luxury hotels. These findings would
   have some practical implications for luxury hotels and their marketers.},
