   International-Association-for-Engineering-Geology-and-the-Environment,
   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {Issues regarding recycling and transportation of soil generated from
   excavation in connection with urban development has become very serious
   in highly urbanized cities. Consequently, studies on a system which can
   effectively manage the excavated surplus soil provided by all
   construction work for reuse as backfilling material have become
   essential to city planing. Environmental problems also arise from
   unplanned dumping and transportation. An automatic dynamic exchange
   system of surplus soil is proposed. This system is based on the soil
   database of the area, a special soil classification system and Internet
   which is an advanced information exchange networks. On line recycling
   process is the main advantage of our proposed system over traditional
   soil recycling procedures.},
