Note = {14th International AIDS Conference, BARCELONA, SPAIN, JUL 07-12, 2002},
Organization = {Univ N Carolina; Gen Clin Res Ctr; UNC Ctr AIDS Res; Natl Inst Hlth;
   Swiss Natl AIDS Res Program; Bristol-Myers Squibb Co; Boehringer
   Ingelheim; GlaxoWellcome Res \& Dev, HIV Antiviral Res},
Abstract = {To adequately address the vulnerability of adolescent girls to HIV/AIDS,
   STDs, unwanted pregnancies, emotional and physical coercion in an urban
   slum merely addressing the girls is not enough. Traditional beliefs and
   patriarchal mindset of the environment in which the girls live also need
   to be addressed.
   Swaasthya developed a reproductive and sexual health intervention that
   worked with the girls and their immediate environment through IEC,
   skills building modules and social support groups.
   Results show that the girls with higher knowledge of reproductive,
   sexual health and legal issues, being the participant of Skills Building
   Modules and social support groups are more likely to have high perceived
   self-determination on issues concerning marriage and child bearing.},
