Note = {International Conference on Business, Management, Tourism and
   Hospitality (BIZMATOUR), Malacca, MALAYSIA, MAY 12-14, 2015},
Abstract = {Mobile learning nowadays is beyond the delivery of learning materials by
   the means of mobile devices that can be accessed anywhere at any given
   time. It becomes crucial when it has been accepted all over the world
   and adopted as one of learning strategies, either in formal or informal
   way in lifelong learning. This study was conducted to identify the
   perception of learner in exploiting their mobile devices for learning
   process either formally or informally. In detail, the objective is to
   measure whether the learner believes in the security of mobile platform
   for learning, the reliability on mobile services used for learning and
   trust on the mobile device and privacy of the mobile technology. These
   independent variables were analyzed to determine the relationship with
   users's loyalty and the results showed that only three independent
   variables which are reliability on mobile services used for learning,
   trust on the mobile device and privacy of the mobile technology that are
   proven to be influential in predicting user loyalty.},
