Abstract = {The Holistic Sustainability Evaluation Framework for Chinese Cities
   discusses the overlapping worldviews of the east and west to provide
   better understanding on how systems theory could be applied on
   sustainability evaluation methods, based on the indigenous philosophies
   of China. After collecting the qualitative data of thirteen large urban
   design projects in four distinct Chinese cities, this paper tries to
   find out how the traditional philosophy and western models were
   underpinning the urban practices in Chinese cities, and to further
   establish the sustainability evaluation model. The future work is to
   validate this framework by testing an external case in China. (C) 2011
