   ELECTR NETWORK, SEP 26-OCT 02, 2020},
Organization = {Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers; Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers Geoscience
   \& Remote Sensing Soc},
Abstract = {Real-time embedded vision tasks require extraction of complex geometric
   and morphological features from the raw 3D point cloud acquired using
   range scanning systems like lidar. radar etc. and depth cameras. Such
   applications are found in autonomous navigation, surveying, 3D mapping
   and localization tasks such as automatic target recognition (ATR).
   Typically, a dataset acquired during surveying by remote sensing lidar
   scanners, known as point cloud, is (1) huge in size and requires a big
   chunk of memory for processing at a single instance and. (2) experiences
   missing information due to rapid change in orientation of the sensor
   while scanning. In our work, we are addressing both the issues
   combinedly by proposing an online point cloud super-resolution approach
   for translating a low dimensional point cloud to a high dimensional
   dense point cloud by learning dictionaries in the low-dimensional
   subspace. We are presenting our approach for an urban road scenario by
   reconstructing dense point clouds of 3D objects and comparing results
   based on PSNR and Hausdorff distance.},
