   multi-source and multi-scale},
Booktitle = {2008 PROCEEDINGS OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY AND ENVIRONMENTAL SYSTEM
   SCIENCES: ITESS 2008, VOL 3},
Year = {2008},
Pages = {323-328},
Note = {International Conference on Informational Technology and Environmental
   System Science, Henan Polytechn Univ, Jiaozuo, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY
   15-17, 2008},
Abstract = {Building polygons and road nets are primary features of urban spatial
   data. Their quickly updating and multi-scale expression are the key
   issues for urban spatial database updating, management and service. A
   method for urban spatial data updating based on multi-source and
   multi-scale data is presented in the paper. QuickBird image data is
   orthorectified by DEM and control points measured by GPS, and then the
   outline of DOR features is traced by ERDAS Imagine 8.7. The change
   information between DOR and DLG is detected and the mapping relation of
   their features is got. At last, the. features of DLG are updated by the
   means of generalization according to the mapping relation, and the
   results show that the method is reasonable and feasible.},
