   Informat Assoc, Lyon, FRANCE, AUG 25-30, 2019},
Organization = {French Assoc Med Informat},
Abstract = {Understanding public risk perceptions, and how these affect behavior, is
   critical to public health's ability to leverage technology for risk
   communications. However, little is known about Zika virus risk
   perceptions. We addressed this gap by analyzing nationally
   representative (US.) survey data. Our results suggest that a minority of
   US. adults perceive Zika to be a major threat (13\%), and only about
   15\% have taken protective actions. Our findings have implications for
   improving technology-supported risk communication.},
