   07-09, 2017},
Organization = {Malaysian Tech Scientist Assoc},
Abstract = {The aim of the study is to identify the employees' perceptions on green
   environmental dimensions. The respondents in this study are the
   employees' at managerial and operational level from various
   manufacturing and industrial companies in Johor Bahru, Johor State,
   Malaysia. This study employed the survey method by using a questionnaire
   to the focused group that consists of 284 respondents at the managerial
   and operational level in manufacturing and industrial companies. The
   green environmental dimensions of that was determined in this study are
   waste management, sustainable resources management, design products and
   material for sustain ability, and sustainable product development.
   Results showed that the highest total average score is 36 percent
   agreement on waste management and followed by sustainable product
   development with 35 percent agreement, sustainable resource management
   is 34 percent and design product and material for sustainability is 30
   percent agreement. The results suggest that the manufacturing and
   industrial companies at Johor Bahru, Johor State, Malaysia specifically
   must do the implementation and practices on green environmental
   dimensions to enhance the environmental sustainability and efficiency on
   their business operation and enhance the environmental quality of life.},
